KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp23 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ print returned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ and clang++ (GCC 16 for C++23 and C++26) accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  With the libstdc++ 16 headers, CBMC did not finish
within 300 s: vprint_nonunicode formats into the FILE's own buffer through
glibc internals CBMC does not model.  It is now modelled as libstdc++'s
buffered variant (format into a string, then fwrite, [print.fun]/16-17), with
models of system_error's categories for the failing write
(cpp11_system_error_generic_category).  About 60 s.
